# clang-tidy configuration for the unit tests
#
# Google Test makes each TEST_F() body a subclass of its fixture, so a
# fixture shares its state with its tests through protected members, as
# Google Test's documentation does. Making them private would only add an
# accessor for each. Otherwise this uses the top-level configuration.
---
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks:
  - -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes
  - -cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes
